.TH LIBMPQ__FILE_VERIFY_EX 3 2026-11-13 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__file_verify_ex \- report member checksum coverage and mismatches
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__file_verify_ex("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *" "archive,"
.BI "        uint32_t " "file_number,"
.BI "        const char *" "filename,"
.BI "        uint32_t " "verify_flags,"
.BI "        uint32_t *" "checked,"
.BI "        uint32_t *" "unavailable,"
.BI "        uint32_t *" "mismatches"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Verify one selected canonical member using the existing LIBMPQ_VERIFY_SECTOR_CRC,
LIBMPQ_VERIFY_FILE_CRC32, LIBMPQ_VERIFY_FILE_MD5 and LIBMPQ_VERIFY_RAW_MD5 bits.
Unknown bits are rejected. Zero flags perform no checks after reader, file
number and output-pointer validation.
.PP
The optional filename is synchronous borrowed basename-derived key context,
not member selection. Resolve exact locale/platform identities with
.BR libmpq__file_number_from_identity (3)
first. Reliable contradictory filename identities are rejected; otherwise the
name is a caller key hint, not proof of filename provenance. NULL retains
anonymous key recovery. Supplied key context is isolated from the parent cache.
KEY uses MPQ-relative offsets, including in embedded archives.
.SS Coverage
On success checked contains performed comparisons, unavailable contains absent,
inapplicable or partially available checks, and mismatches is a subset of
checked. Both coverage outputs are subsets of verify_flags, and their union
is verify_flags. Partial sector coverage sets both checked and unavailable.
A complete matching result requires all of the following:
.nf
    status == 0
    checked == verify_flags
    unavailable == 0
    mismatches == 0
.fi
.PP
Sector checks compare packed, decrypted sector bytes before decoding. Missing
sector tables, zero/all-ones entries and inapplicable storage are unavailable.
At least one usable comparison sets checked; any missing sector sets unavailable.
.PP
Missing attributes, omitted physical rows, absent checksum arrays and all-zero
MD5 placeholders are unavailable. Valid BET-only members have no fabricated
classic attributes. Ordinary CRC32 zero is available, including for empty data.
Zero CRC32 placeholders are unavailable only for the attributes self row or a
recognized weak signature member. Legacy file_verify retains literal comparisons.
.PP
Logical CRC32/MD5 are unavailable when actual ADPCM decoding is lossy: current
attributes do not establish decoded-byte checksum provenance. Lossless blocks
and files still compare normally. Sector and raw checks remain independent.
Malformed metadata and read, key or decode failures remain operational errors.
.PP
Raw MD5 compares stored MPQ payload chunks after MPQE transport decoding without
requiring plaintext keys. Older versions, zero raw size, zero stored length,
and delete markers are unavailable. Nonzero v4 raw size establishes expected
coverage for every eligible nonempty physical member. Missing or truncated
required arrays are format/read errors, including when the payload ends at the
archive boundary or another live structure starts at the expected array.
Zero-filled bytes are compared as digests, never treated as absence. Overlapping
or out-of-bounds required arrays remain errors. These are physical member checks,
not verification of a reconstructed patch result. A matching unkeyed MD5 establishes
neither digest provenance nor cryptographic authenticity.
.PP
A private immutable layout index is built lazily and reused. Preprocessing costs
O(N log N) time and O(N) memory; each member overlap query costs O(log N).
Reader clones share completed indexes and may outlive their parents. Allocation
or construction failure publishes no partial index and leaves the handle usable.
Index and clone lifetime operations retain the existing external serialization
requirements; indexing does not establish that every stored range is valid.
.PP
Verification uses one decoded-block buffer and one shared traversal. SINGLE_UNIT
storage may require a buffer as large as that logical member. This operation
does not establish signature trust, structural metadata coverage or whole-archive
integrity. VERIFY_ALL requests all member checks; it does not promise availability.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
/* number was resolved for data/sample.bin in the open reader.
 * The filename supplies key context for that member. */
int32_t
check_sample_coverage(
    mpq_archive_s *archive, uint32_t number, int *matched
)
{
    const uint32_t requested = LIBMPQ_VERIFY_FILE_MD5 | LIBMPQ_VERIFY_RAW_MD5;
    uint32_t checked, unavailable, mismatches;
    int32_t status = libmpq__file_verify_ex(
        archive, number, "data/sample.bin", requested,
        &checked, &unavailable, &mismatches
    );
    if (status == 0)
        *matched = checked == requested && unavailable == 0 && mismatches == 0;
    return status;
}
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
Zero means verification completed, even with unavailable checks or mismatches.
Negative LIBMPQ_ERROR_* values report operational failures. All three required
output pointers are cleared on failure when valid. Invalid pointers or file
numbers return EXIST; writable handles return NOT_INITIALIZED; unknown flags
and malformed metadata return FORMAT. Read, allocation, decryption and decoding
failures retain their established errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__file_verify (3),
.BR libmpq__block_verify (3),
.BR libmpq__file_attributes (3),
.BR libmpq__file_number_from_identity (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_verify (3)
